#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/using-components.md:2
msgid "Work with components"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/using-components.md:4
msgid ""
"A snap *component* is part of a snap that has been declared as optional. A "
"snap component may then be either installed or not installed alongside its "
"host snap. See {ref}`How components work <explanation-how-snaps-work-snap-"
"components>` for further details."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/using-components.md:7
msgid "Component support requires _snapd 2.67+_."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/using-components.md:9
msgid "Installing components"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/using-components.md:11
msgid "Components can be installed with the snap install command:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/using-components.md:13
msgid "snap install my-snap+comp1+comp2\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/using-components.md:17
msgid ""
"The syntax `<snap_name>+<comp_1>+...+<comp_N>` will be used to refer to "
"components from the command line."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/using-components.md:19
msgid ""
"The above command will install _my-snap_ alongside components _comp1_ and "
"_comp2_. If the snap is already installed, the command will instead install "
"only the missing components."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/using-components.md:21
msgid ""
"Once installed, the (asserted) components will refresh when new revisions "
"are available in the store, in the same way as for snaps."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/using-components.md:23
msgid ""
"It is also possible to install components from local files. If {ref}"
"`unasserted <explanation-security-assertions>`, they can be installed only "
"if the host snap is unasserted too and you will need to use the --dangerous "
"flag:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/using-components.md:25
msgid "snap install --dangerous ./my-snap+comp1+comp2_1.0.comp\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/using-components.md:29
msgid ""
"When refreshing a snap, all components will refresh to the new revisions "
"tuple. If the new snap revision does not define some components defined in "
"the previously installed snap and that are currently installed, those "
"components will be removed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/using-components.md:31
msgid ""
"Refreshing an unasserted snap requires  new component builds to be installed "
"manually."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/using-components.md:33
msgid "Updating components"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/using-components.md:35
msgid ""
"It is also possible to refresh a snap and install a component at the same "
"time:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/using-components.md:37
msgid "snap refresh my-snap+comp1\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/using-components.md:41
msgid "Listing components"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/using-components.md:43
msgid ""
"The `snap components` command is used to list the components installed and "
"available on the system:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/using-components.md:45
msgid ""
"$ snap components\n"
"Component                    Status     Type\n"
"snap-with-comps+one          installed  standard\n"
"snap-with-comps+two          installed  standard\n"
"snap-with-comps+three        available  standard\n"
"other-snap-with-comps+one    installed  standard\n"
"other-snap-with-comps+two    installed  standard\n"
"other-snap-with-comps+three  available  standard\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/using-components.md:56
msgid ""
"A snap name can be optionally provided to filters the list of reported "
"components to those only associated with the provided snap:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/using-components.md:58
msgid ""
"$ snap components snap-with-comps\n"
"Component                \tStatus \tType\n"
"snap-with-comps+one      \tinstalled  standard\n"
"snap-with-comps+two      \tinstalled  standard\n"
"snap-with-comps+three    \tavailable  standard\n"
"Note that there are some plans for a \"snap component\" subcommand, but that "
"is not yet implemented and there are talks of changing its design.\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/using-components.md:67
msgid ""
"Using the `snap info` command displays a summary of the ratio of installed "
"components to components available from the store. If both installed and "
"available components are zero, the summary will be omitted"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/using-components.md:69
msgid ""
"$ snap info qwen-vl \n"
"name:      qwen-vl\n"
"summary:   Qwen VL inference snap\n"
"...\n"
"installed:          2.5            (248) 332MB -\n"
"components: 4/14\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/using-components.md:78
msgid "Introspecting components"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/using-components.md:80
msgid ""
"In order to view information regarding an installed/available component(s), "
"the `snap component` command may be used."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/using-components.md:82
msgid ""
"$ snap component qwen-vl+llamacpp\n"
"component: qwen-vl+llamacpp\n"
"type: standard\n"
"summary: llama.cpp Engine using default CPU instruction sets\n"
"description: |\n"
"  LLM inference in C/C++\n"
"installed: b5794 (240) 30MB\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/using-components.md:92
msgid ""
"The last line, `installed:` is only printed if a component is installed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/using-components.md:94
msgid ""
"$ snap component qwen-vl+llamacpp+model-qwen2-5-vl-3b-instruct-q4-k-m\n"
"component: qwen-vl+llamacpp\n"
"type: standard\n"
"summary: llama.cpp Engine using default CPU instruction sets\n"
"description: |\n"
"  LLM inference in C/C++\n"
"installed: b5794 (247) 31MB\n"
"---\n"
"component: qwen-vl+model-qwen2-5-vl-3b-instruct-q4-k-m\n"
"type: standard\n"
"summary: Qwen 2.5 VL 3B Q4\n"
"description: |\n"
"  Quantized model with 3B parameters in gguf format with Q4_K_M weight "
"encoding\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/using-components.md:110
msgid "Removing components"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/using-components.md:112
msgid ""
"To remove only the components, use the \"remove\" command, followed by the "
"snap and component names:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/using-components.md:114
msgid "snap remove my-snap+comp1+comp2\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/using-components.md:118
msgid "To remove the snap plus any installed components, just remove the snap:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/using-components.md:120
msgid "snap remove my-snap\n"
msgstr ""
